### StudyMind API smoke test.
### Works with the "REST Client" extension in VS Code (click "Send Request" above each block).
@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Health (public): shows whether AI is configured
GET {{host}}/api/health

### 2. Register (returns a token) - copy the token into @token below
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "shrey@example.com", "password": "password123", "name": "Shrey", "program": "BTech CSE" }

@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### 3. Write the timetable in plain words; the AI works out the subjects
PUT {{host}}/api/timetable
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Monday: 9-10 DBMS, 10-11 Operating Systems, 2-4 Machine Learning Lab\nTuesday: 9-10 Cloud Computing, 10-11 AI\nWednesday: 9-10 DBMS, 11-12 MAD" }

### 4. Add an exam (a subject is created automatically from subjectName)
POST {{host}}/api/exams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subjectName": "DBMS", "title": "DBMS Mid-sem", "examDate": "2026-11-25", "maxMarks": 100, "importance": 4 }

### 5. Past result: marks obtained (feeds the "weak subject" logic)
POST {{host}}/api/exams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subjectName": "AI", "title": "AI Quiz 1", "examDate": "2026-10-01", "maxMarks": 50, "obtainedMarks": 21 }

### 6. Generate the study plan
POST {{host}}/api/study-plan/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Exam summary (how many, averages per subject)
GET {{host}}/api/exams/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Upload a PDF: use the frontend, or curl:
###   curl.exe -H "Authorization: Bearer TOKEN" -F "file=@notes.pdf" http://localhost:8080/api/documents

### 9. Create a chat and ask a question (replace CHAT_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/chats
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###
POST {{host}}/api/chats/CHAT_ID/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "What is the difference between 3NF and BCNF?" }

### 10. Generate flashcards / a quiz from a document (replace DOC_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/documents/DOC_ID/flashcards/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "count": 12 }

###
POST {{host}}/api/documents/DOC_ID/quizzes/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "count": 8, "difficulty": "medium" }

### 11. Everything the Home screen needs
GET {{host}}/api/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
